      "id": "l01",
      "start": 0.4,
      "end": 4.193,
      "text": "Your eyes can't see this remote's light. So why can your phone camera?",
      "words": 13,
      "words_per_s": 3.43,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.2
    },
    {
      "id": "l02",
      "start": 4.6,
      "end": 11.167,
      "text": "Remotes blink infrared, light just past the red end your eyes detect, in a quick code the TV reads.",
      "words": 19,
      "words_per_s": 2.89,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.6
    },
    {
      "id": "l03",
      "start": 11.6,
      "end": 16.311,
      "text": "Many camera sensors respond to that infrared, so the blinks show up on screen.",
      "words": 14,
      "words_per_s": 2.97,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 17.6
    },
    {
      "id": "l04",
      "start": 16.8,
      "end": 23.544,
      "text": "Remote not working? Aim it at the camera and press a button. No flicker? Try new batteries, or another camera.",
      "words": 20,
      "words_per_s": 2.97,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 15.7
    },
    {
      "id": "l05",
      "start": 26.35,
      "end": 29.639,
      "text": "Download Recall for learning any new subject with AI.",
      "words": 9,
      "words_per_s": 2.74,
      "voice_over_bed_db": 16.7
    }
  ],
